<article class="env-lemma" id="0B79">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B79">Lemma <span data-tag="0B79">42.33.3</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Let $(\mathcal{L}, s, i : D \to X)$ be a triple as in Definition <a href="/tag/02T8" data-tag="02T8">42.29.1</a>. Then the rule that to $f : X' \to X$ assigns $(i')^* : \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ k(X') \to \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _{k - 1}(D')$ where $D' = D \times _ X X'$ is a bivariant class of degree $1$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Lemmas <a href="/tag/02TO" data-tag="02TO">42.30.2</a>, <a href="/tag/02TA" data-tag="02TA">42.29.8</a>, <a href="/tag/0B71" data-tag="0B71">42.29.9</a>, and <a href="/tag/0B73" data-tag="0B73">42.30.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>